  "narrative": "Kampaamo Kultalanka Oy, February 2025 (the first clean run of the Finnish test book, 2026-09-08). ONE document — the Nets monthly report, a koontilasku listing four weekly card settlements VKO5–VKO8, each with its own gross, transaction count, 1.10 % fee and net, plus a total — and FOUR bank credits, one per week at that week's NET. Before RT-21 the payout lane's one-to-one contract forced the model to tag every credit partial_payment; authorizeMatch then held each with below_floor + insufficient_separation + above_materiality_ceiling and 10 206,48 EUR of card sales rested on nobody. The contract (prompt §2): bank line ↔ statement row, full settlement at that row's NET, exact; proposals against DIFFERENT rows are not ties; the document converges when every row is settled. Decoys: a customer transfer equal to VKO5's GROSS (a credit equal to a row's gross is NOT that row) and an unrelated refund credit.",
  "provenance": "RECONSTRUCTED from the 2026-09-08 receipts (prompt docs/prompt-2026-09-08-rt-21-koontilasku-settlement-rows.md §1/§5): statement net 10 206,48; fee 1,10 % = 113,52 (gross 10 320,00); VKO5 gross 2 480,00; the note that VKO9 settles 3.3. The VKO6–VKO8 grosses and the transaction counts were NOT recorded in the receipts and are chosen so the rows foot; replace them (and document_text) with the printed figures from `14 Nets kuukausiraportti 02-2025.pdf` on the laptop appliance when scoring the real extraction.",
